lifeos-nix patch f-inference-provider — local model server, with Anthropic as fallback

PROBLEM
  LifeOS can only talk to Anthropic. `claude` is the sole model client (interactive launch,
  `lifeos -p`, every Inference.ts call spawn it), and Inference.ts actively deletes
  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, so even a hand-set local endpoint is scrubbed. There is no way to run
  on a local LLM server, and no way to keep Anthropic as a safety net if one is used.

FIX
  One switch in the USER-zone config, LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/LIFEOS_CONFIG.toml:

    [inference]
    mode = "local-with-fallback"     # anthropic-only | local-with-fallback | local-only
    [inference.local]
    base_url  = "http://host:port"   # must speak Anthropic /v1/messages
    model     = "name"               # all tiers; [inference.local.models] overrides per tier
    token_env = "VAR"                # optional

  - NEW LIFEOS/TOOLS/InferenceProvider.ts: validate the section, build the local env overlay
    (BASE_URL, AUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_{FABLE,OPUS,SONNET,HAIKU}_MODEL,
    SMALL_FAST_MODEL, SUBAGENT_MODEL; local-only adds DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC), health
    check GET {base}/v1/models, append events to MEMORY/OBSERVABILITY/inference-provider.jsonl.
  - LifeosConfig.ts: loadRawLifeosConfig() — the TOML without identity validation, uncached.
  - Inference.ts: inference() picks the target; local-with-fallback retries once on
    Anthropic when the local attempt fails; local-only fails closed. The local target maps
    the tier (alias or pinned id) to the local model, verifies the executed model against
    that name, and skips the max→high rung retry when both rungs map to one local model.
  - lifeos.ts: launch and -p health-check once per launch; healthy → local, down + fallback →
    Anthropic with a stderr notice, down + local-only → refuse (exit 1).

  The Anthropic path is the upstream code: the local env is layered on top of each caller's
  existing scrub, never replacing it. No section, no file → anthropic-only. A present but
  invalid section REFUSES (launcher exits, inference() errors): a typo of "local-only" must
  never quietly route work to Anthropic.

VERIFIED GOTCHA (why AUTH_TOKEN is always set on the local target)
  With only ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL set, Claude Code sends the subscription OAuth bearer token to
  that URL. Measured 2026-10-04 against a header-recording server: BASE_URL alone → the OAuth
  token arrived; with the placeholder AUTH_TOKEN → 16 requests, no `sk-ant-` value in any
  header. ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN outranks OAuth, so a server without auth still gets
  "lifeos-local-no-auth", never the subscription credential.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One new file + three edited (Inference.ts, LifeosConfig.ts, lifeos.ts). lifeos.ts hunks are
  disjoint from f-launcher-cwd (import line, helper after error(), the two spawn env lines).
  Out of scope (ISA Step 7 fog): cross-vendor lanes under local-only; egress-test K = local host.

VERIFICATION
  tests/inference-provider/run.sh — 25 tests: resolution + refusals, env overlay, Inference.ts
  end to end with a recording fake `claude`, launcher against an up/down fake server. Five
  mutations of this patch (local-only falling back, no placeholder token, launcher not
  refusing, health always ok, absent section not anthropic-only) each turn the suite red.

